<div class="guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Provider comparison">
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col">Provider</th>
<th scope="col">Compose with the shell</th>
<th scope="col">What differs from a host tool</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-gh">gh</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Read PR metadata → filter with <code>jq</code> → comment with a separate grant.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">GitHub-shaped commands, not the GitHub CLI; no arbitrary API passthrough.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-ripgrep">ripgrep</a> / <a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-python">python</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Search supplied documents or transform structured data in RustPython.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">Document paths are labels, not host files. Python has selected imports, not pip.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-curl">curl</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Fetch an allowed HTTPS URL into a byte-stream pipeline.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">GET only; destination and byte limits still apply to model-chosen URLs.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-turso-sql">turso</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Store and query records with the Rust Turso SQL engine.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">Broker-owned durable files; exceeding write budgets can leave a database unreadable.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-gpt-image">gpt-image</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Generate or edit PNGs using a ChatGPT subscription.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">Undocumented upstream endpoints; install a current component with the matching asset contract.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-vm">vm / ssh</a></th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Run browser or Python tools in a separately deployed Firecracker VM through vm-runner.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">The command word is not SSH. Broker policy gates the runner API; the guest has its own image and isolation boundary.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="workbench-example">
<div>
<h3>Read a PR, keep two fields</h3>
<p>Illustrative script for Dekopon’s <code>bash</code> tool, not your terminal. Replace the repository and PR number; install a compatible <code>gh</code> component and grant <code>gh.pull-request.read</code> first.</p>
</div>
<pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Illustrative read-only GitHub workflow"><code>set -e
set -o pipefail
gh pr view 7 -R owner/repo | jq '{title, state}'</code>
</pre>
</div>
<p>The result is an object with <code>title</code> and <code>state</code>, not a file checkout. A missing session grant exits 127; a broker denial exits 126. <a href="/guides/runtime/#workflow">Prerequisites and failure behavior</a>.</p>
<p>Current releases use <code>provider@0.4.0</code>; install them explicitly because the core image does not bundle these providers. <a href="/guides/provider-sdk/">Build and test a provider</a> · <a href="/guides/access/">Configure access</a>
</p>
<h3>Jobs and reusable skills</h3>
<p>Routes can opt into bounded background jobs. Installed providers can run child scripts under the caller's existing limits, and agents with a storage grant can save learned skills. <a href="/guides/runtime/">See the runtime controls</a>.</p>
<p>Set per-agent token budgets and inspect broker-granted commands through the optional <a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-console/releases/tag/v0.8.0">console</a>. <a href="/inference/">Model setup and limits</a>.</p>
</div>
